# AT4130 KV230 Motor Settings (XML Export)

This file should be filled with actual XML export from VESC Tool.

## How to Export:
1. Connect VESC to VESC Tool
2. Go to **Configuration** tab
3. Click **Export** → **Export Current Configuration**
4. Save as `AT4130_KV230_vesc_mcconf.xml`

## Expected Contents:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<MCConfiguration>
    <!-- Basic Motor Settings -->
    <si-motor-poles>14</si-motor-poles>
    <si-gear-ratio>1.0</si-gear-ratio>
    
    <!-- Current Limits -->
    <l-current-max>30</l-current-max>
    <l-current-min>-30</l-current-min>
    <l-max-erpm>50000</l-max-erpm>
    <l-min-erpm>-50000</l-min-erpm>
    
    <!-- Battery Settings -->
    <l-battery-cut-start>20.4</l-battery-cut-start>
    <l-battery-cut-end>18.0</l-battery-cut-end>
    <si-battery-cells>6</si-battery-cells>
    
    <!-- FOC Parameters (if using FOC) -->
    <foc-motor-r>???</foc-motor-r>
    <foc-motor-l>???</foc-motor-l>
    <foc-motor-flux-linkage>???</foc-motor-flux-linkage>
    
    <!-- Openloop Settings for Starter Mode -->
    <foc-openloop-rpm>1000</foc-openloop-rpm>
    <foc-sl-openloop-time>0.05</foc-sl-openloop-time>
    
    <!-- Other Settings -->
    <l-max-duty>0.95</l-max-duty>
    <l-min-duty>-0.95</l-min-duty>
</MCConfiguration>
```

## Post-Export Steps:
1. Replace `???` with actual measured values
2. Adjust `si-motor-poles` based on motor label/datasheet
3. Adjust current limits based on actual motor rating
4. Test at low power first (5-10% duty cycle)
